CLASS:: RedMstGUI
SUMMARY:: gui window for RedMst
CATEGORIES:: Red>redMst
RELATED:: Classes/RedMst, Classes/RedMstGUI2, Classes/RedMstGUI3

DESCRIPTION::
Use this class for lowest CPU usage. link::Classes/RedMstGUI2:: and link::Classes/RedMstGUI3:: adds metronome and transport view but takes a little bit more to update.

The GUI takes the following keyboard commands...
table::
## escape key || go to next section. Same as code::RedMst.next::
## left arrow key || go to previous section. Same as code::RedMst.prev::
## right arrow key || go to next section. Same as code::RedMst.next::
## space key || toggle RedMst play and stop
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new

ARGUMENT:: size
Fontsize. The default is 24.

ARGUMENT:: skin
An optional GUI.skin. Without a skin, the window uses the shared dark or light theme. Explicit custom skins remain unchanged by shared theme switches and omit the theme button.

ARGUMENT:: seq
The RedSeq controlled by this window.

METHOD:: theme
Get or set the shared theme using code::\dark:: or code::\light::. The default is code::\dark::. Setting it updates all open windows that use the shared theme; new windows inherit the current selection. The small button in the top-right corner of each themed window changes this same setting.

The theme is shared by RedMstGUI, RedMstGUI2, RedMstGUI3, RedMstSessionGUI, and RedMstArrangementGUI. It lasts for the current language session and resets after class-library recompilation. Switching themes does not change playback or mixer values.

CODE::
RedMstGUI.theme = \light;
RedMstGUI.theme; // -> light
RedMstGUI.theme = \dark;
::

After updating these classes, recompile the SuperCollider class library, reload your score setup, and reopen the windows.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

PRIVATE:: initRedMstGUI, prInitInterface, prInitMetro, prInitUser, prInitTask, prInitCleanUp

METHOD:: dur
How often to redraw the window in beats. The default is 0.25 which means every 16th note. It uses code::RedMst.clock::.

METHOD:: win
Handle to the actual window created.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
//--simple example
(
s.waitForBoot{
RedMst.clear;
RedMst.clock= TempoClock(140/60);
RedMst.quant= 8;
RedMstGUI(20);

RedTrack(
	\bass,
	Pbind(\degree, Pseq([0, 5], inf), \octave, 4),
	#[0, 1, 2, 3]								
);
RedTrack(
	\melody,
	Pbind(\degree, Pseq([0, 5, 2, 3, 3, 1], inf), \dur, Pseq([0.25, 0.25, 0.5], inf)),
	#[1, 2, 5]
);
RedTrack(
	\melody2,
	Pbind(\degree, Pseq([7, 6, 4, 3], inf), \dur, 2, \octave, 6),
	#[2, 3]
);
}
)

RedMst.play;
RedMst.next;
RedMst.next;
RedMst.quant= 2;

RedMstGUI(64);						//add more guis
RedMstGUI(24, GUI.skins.default);
RedMstGUI(9);

RedMst.next;
RedMst.stop;
RedMst.clear;
::
